Part 2: The big refactor

capitolo 5 physics system
- physics system that consumes the positions and hitboxes from a Config.gameData and all the speeds of objects.

capitolo 6 render and animations are separate things!
so if i have an animationsystem i can effectively register there just the animation and then the animation
shares Renderer.Image with the sprite in the renderer so effectively the renderer only treats pos and images.
now animations can have events linked to them, like ended or stuff
- render system that consumes positions and gets fed images and does all the rendering and updating of animations
in a more elegan way:
> an optimization: we can make the renderer draw identical for all objects if they all have the same properties
that is a correct abstraction of an image: Renderer.Image(img, offset, size);
in the phase of update instead we have a separate array with the animations and update only them 
so we never do ifs in the renderer.draw(). the updateAnimations method will update the animations in O(n) time.

